934ebcae9e0115c96bc92a6a5859b6ab2ea75fd8fc7887a4","bytes":20860,"original_dimensions":[1296,968]}],"gold":"A","prediction":"D","correct":false,"forced":false,"output":"<spatial_thinking><abs_vis_token><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad></abs_vis_token>To determine the position of the box relative to the shelves and whiteboard, we need to analyze the spatial layout from multiple images.\n\nP<abs_vis_token><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad></abs_vis_token>- In Image 1, the view is from a corner of the room showing a desk with a monitor, two chairs, a black mini-fridge, and a whiteboard on the left wall. The shelves are visible in the background to the right.\n  \n<|<abs_vis_token><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad></abs_vis_token>- In Image 2, the camera moves closer to the whiteboard and fridge, focusing on the left side of the room. The whiteboard is now prominent, and the fridge is in front of it. The shelves are no longer visible.\n\n</spatial_thinking>\n\n<thinking><abs_vis_token><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad><abs_vis_token_pad></abs_vis_token>- From Image 1, if you stand at the shelves facing the whiteboard, you are looking toward the left wall where the whiteboard is mounted.\n   We can infer that the box (a cardboard box with blue items inside) is located near the base of the whiteboard or along the adjacent wall, as seen in Image 23 and Image 24.\n   In Image 23, the whiteboard is visible, and below it, near the bottom right corner of the frame, there’s a cardboard box leaning against the wall next to a power strip and some rolled-up materials.\n   Since the shelves are to the right of the whiteboard when facing it (as seen in Image 1), and the box is located near the whiteboard’s lower edge, it must be to the **right** of the whiteboard from the perspective of someone standing at the shelves and facing the whiteboard.\n\n</thinking>\n\n<answer>D</answer><|im_end|>","latent":{"blocks":4,"body_tokens":64,"events":[{"phase":"spatial_thinking","boundary":0,"kind":"section_entry","body_tokens":16},{"phase":"spatial_thinking","boundary":1,"kind":"source_step","body_tokens":16},{"phase":"spatial_thinking","boundary":2,"kind":"source_step","body_tokens":16},{"phase":"thinking","boundary":0,"kind":"section_entry","body_tokens":16}]},"prompt_sha256":"16286a04a6daaebd4ebdd006b16649668e83ff9cfde3bc1015e381160b1e3ef8","rl":null}
